<title>SINGAPORE: SIMEX Nikkei futures closed for Tokyo holiday.</title>
<headline>SIMEX Nikkei futures closed for Tokyo holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The SIMEX Nikkei futures market was closed on Monday due to a Japanese holiday. Trading will resume on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The lead Nikkei 225 September contract lost 280 points to end at 20,575 last Friday as players squared their positions and took profits ahead of the long weekend.</p>
<p>Dealers said the contract should be supported around 20,100-20,250 with resistance seen above 20,600.</p>
<p>-- Sonali Desai (65-8703090)</p>
</text>
